 "sentences": [
  "One of the key rules is that we always end function names with '_b'.",
  "Consistency in code is crucial for collaboration and maintainability.",
  "Now, as you settle into your role, feel free to reach out to me with any questions or concerns.",
  "I can put you in touch with the right people if you'd like to explore ways to contribute.",
  "For function names, please end them with '_d'.",
  "This helps us maintain consistency and easily identify these functions in our codebases.",
  "Additionally, always add the '@timer_class' decorator from the 'pedantic' module to all your classes.",
  "This helps us profile the execution time of our code, which is valuable for performance optimization.",
  "If you have any questions or need further clarification, don't hesitate to reach out.",
  "We're all here to support each other and ensure we're delivering the best possible code.",
  "Going forward, I'd like you to work from home no more than twice a week.",
  "It's important for your growth and collaboration with the team to have a presence in the office.",
  "First, always add comments to your code.",
  "Clear and concise comments help other developers understand your logic and make collaboration smoother.",
  "Indeed.",
  "Also, remember to utilize annotations for your functions.",
  "Keep up the good work, and don't hesitate to reach out if any questions or challenges arise."
 ],
